"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8804},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":33254,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.033329,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":13066,"cacheReadInputTokens":176982,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55340,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.761061,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"# Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Bounded objective\\nReconcile the k-12Harness *documentation and help surfaces* — entry-point CLI help/docstrings (`run.py`, `demo.py`, and the module entry points `python -m evals.live` / `python -m harness.usage`), operational guidance (`RUNBOOK.md`, `README.md`), and release documentation (`releases/`) — so their prose matches the implemented reality already recorded in the two Definition Pack references: (1) the implemented pipeline status (M1–M5 build order and what is/ isn't wired), (2) the explicit evaluation stages (deterministic PR-gate tier, manual/nightly live tier reporting pass@k/pass^k, the `--pressure` probe, and the three demo modes), (3) the pinned model / default provider, and (4) the checkpoint/pin compatibility rules. This is a documentation-reconciliation work item: **no runtime behaviour changes** — only help text, docstrings, runbook/README prose, and a release note. Symbol behaviour, provider selection logic, and eval mechanics stay as implemented.\\n\\n## Definition Pack interpretation\\nAuthority boundary = the two references pinned in `manifest.yaml`: `docs/architecture.md` (sha256 d20e51…) and `docs/decisions.md` (sha256 18d2cce…). Both were provided in full. Salient facts the doc surfaces must be reconciled *to*:\\n- **Provider / model (decisions.md ADR-018 → ADR-019).** `claude_account` is the default provider, invoking `claude --print` under the inherited `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, with built-in tools/MCP/session persistence disabled and metered env vars stripped. `anthropic_sdk` is available *only* by explicit `HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk` and is documented as potentially metered. ADR-019 supersedes ADR-018; ADR-018 remains as history. Account plans expose no per-request USD/cache counters, so the harness reports account-plan usage and retains only non-financial step/tool-call/wall-clock ceilings.\\n- **Evaluation stages (decisions.md ADR-007, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015, ADR-017; O-10).** Deterministic tier gates every PR at zero network cost; live tier (`python -m evals.live`, `tests/live/`) is manual/nightly and reports pass@k and pass^k *separately*; `--pressure` (O-10) appends red-team phrasings and writes transcripts for a human to read (it does not grade). `evals/replay.py` runs the full offline production path. Demo (ADR-017) has three modes — `--replay`, `--stub`, and neither-flag (live) — each announced by a tested banner.\\n- **Pipeline status (architecture.md §12; decisions.md O-2, O-4).** M1–M5 milestones; server layer (`server/`) is carried but unwired (O-2); forecasting is registered-but-gated (VC-POC-14, O-4 resolved), not part of MVP.\\n- **Pin / compatibility rules (decisions.md ADR-008, ADR-015 decision 3; ADR-006).** The contract is pinned by hash (`contract/PINNED.json`); a bump is a loud four-step operation (re-pin, regenerate the prompt, regenerate the fixture bundle, re-point cases). The Anthropic SDK is pinned exactly alongside the framework as one compatibility surface (ADR-015-3). Per-model cache minimums (`CACHE_MIN_TOKENS`) are re-verified on model upgrades (ADR-006).\\n\\n## Current implementation\\nEstablished from the authority docs + inventory only (component-repo file bodies were requested but not returned by the host, so their exact current wording is unverified):\\n- Entry points present: `run.py` (CLI), `demo.py` (walked demo), `evals/live.py` (`python -m evals.live`), `harness/usage.py` (`python -m harness.usage report`), `prompts/build_prompt.py` (`--capture`).\\n- Provider adapters exist: `harness/claude_account_cli.py` (ADR-019 default), plus the anthropic_sdk path.\\n- Doc surfaces to reconcile: `README.md`, `RUNBOOK.md`, `releases/` (versioned notes v0.1.0…v1.2.0, `_template.md`, `_next/.gitkeep` staging dir).\\n- Enforcing checks in the inventory: `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py`, `tests/unit/test_demo.py`, `tests/unit/test_usage.py`, the release-note gate (`.claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh` + `.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml`; sibling WI 20260908T113226 shows a `release-note-typed` acceptance check), and the contract pin test `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py`.\\n- **Suspected drift the request targets:** architecture.md §8 still names `claude-sonnet-4-6` as the model and §9 describes API-key/account-bearer auth — text predating ADR-018/019’s move to the Claude CLI subscription provider. Whichever doc surfaces echo §8/§9 (README/RUNBOOK) are the likely stale-model / stale-auth statements to reconcile.\\n\\n## Proposed changes\\nEach file below is in scope; any enforcing file not named here is out of scope and the executor may not implement around it.\\n- **root1:README.md** — Reconcile the top-level description of provider/model, evaluation tiers, and pipeline status: state `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth) as the default provider per ADR-019, `anthropic_sdk` as explicit-and-metered, remove/qualify any stale “anthropic SDK default” or bare “`claude-sonnet-4-6` pinned” claim (subject to the GAP below), and summarise the M1–M5 status honestly (server unwired, forecasting gated). No behaviour claims beyond the ADRs.\\n- **root1:RUNBOOK.md** — Reconcile operator guidance: auth setup (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` inherited, `SHARED_ENV_FILE` machine-level secrets, ADR-011/019), how to run the deterministic tier (pytest, PR gate, zero network), the live tier (`python -m evals.live`, manual/nightly, pass@k and pass^k reported separately), the `--pressure` probe (transcripts must be read by a human), the three demo modes and their banner meaning, provider override (`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`, potentially metered), and the contract/SDK pin-adoption rules (ADR-008 four-step bump; ADR-015-3 SDK+framework as one pinned surface).\\n- **root1:run.py** — Update argparse `help=`/`description` and module docstring for the CLI subcommands so help text names the current provider default and the explicit eval stages; **no logic change**. Enforced by `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py`.\\n- **root1:demo.py** — Align mode/help text and any banner-adjacent prose with ADR-017’s three modes and banner semantics; must not introduce a `def render_*` (ADR-017 property) and must not restate rendering rules. Enforced by `tests/unit/test_demo.py`.\\n- **root1:releases/_next/<slug>.md** — New release note (typed per `root1:releases/_template.md`) recording this documentation reconciliation. Required by the release-note gate (`.claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh`, `.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml`, `release-note-typed` check); must gain a correctly-typed entry or CI blocks the change.\\n\\nEnforcing checks that must be updated in lockstep (in scope):\\n- **root1:tests/unit/test_run_cli.py** — must gain/adjust assertions matching the reconciled `run.py` help/description strings (or continue to pass unchanged if it does not assert on the edited text). If it pins help output verbatim, it must be updated to the new text.\\n- **root1:tests/unit/test_demo.py** — must continue to hold the ADR-017 properties (no `render_*` in `demo.py`, banner present, `demo.GROUPS` partition) and gain/adjust any assertion over edited mode/help text.\\n- **root1:tests/unit/test_usage.py** — in scope only if `harness/usage.py` report help text is edited; must be updated to match, else leave untouched.\\n\\nExplicitly out of scope (do not edit): `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/decisions.md` (the authority; drift within them is a GAP, not an edit target here), `config/settings.py` and provider adapters (behaviour), `contract/PINNED.json` and `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` (no contract bump in this WI).\\n\\n## Verification approach\\n- Run the declared deterministic suite: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` (manifest `k-12Harness.verify`) — must stay green, in particular `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py`, `tests/unit/test_demo.py`, `tests/unit/test_usage.py`, and `tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py` (proves no accidental pin/behaviour change).\\n- Confirm the release-note gate passes: `.claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh` and the `pr-checks` workflow `release-note-typed` step accept the new `releases/_next/<slug>.md`.\\n- Deterministic doc-consistency acceptance: assert README/RUNBOOK no longer state a provider/model contradicting ADR-019, and that they name the deterministic tier, the live `pass@k`/`pass^k` tier, `--pressure`, and the three demo modes. (Analogue of sibling WIs’ `usage-convention-green` / `release-note-typed` dry-run checks.)\\n- No live-tier or network run is required or appropriate for a docs-only change.\\n\\n## Risks, assumptions and gaps\\n- **Assumption (bounding):** the current bodies of `run.py`, `README.md`, `RUNBOOK.md`, `demo.py`, the release notes and the enforcing tests were not returned by the host; exact line-level edit points and whether the CLI tests pin help text verbatim are unverified. The executor must inspect these before editing and treat any verbatim-help assertion as an update target.\\n- **Risk:** editing argparse help text can silently break `test_run_cli.py`/`test_demo.py` if they assert on strings — mitigated by updating those tests in the same change (named in scope).\\n- **Risk:** overstating status (e.g., claiming the server layer or forecasting is live) would re-introduce drift; guidance must mirror O-2 (server unwired) and O-4 (forecasting gated).\\n- **Assumption:** no contract version bump is involved, so `PINNED.json`/pin test stay untouched; if reconciliation prose must quote a pinned model name, it should reference the single source of truth rather than restating a literal that can drift.\\n\\n## Planning gaps\\nGAP: docs/architecture.md §8 (\\\"Model: claude-sonnet-4-6\\\") and §9 (API-key/account-bearer auth) conflict with docs/decisions.md ADR-019 (claude_account/Claude-CLI subscription OAuth as default, ADR-018 superseded) — the authoritative \\\"pinned model\\\"/default-provider statement the doc surfaces must adopt is unresolved between these two Definition Pack sections.\\nGAP: request.md names \\\"checkpoint compatibility rules\\\" but neither Definition Pack reference (docs/architecture.md, docs/decisions.md) defines a \\\"checkpoint\\\" concept; the referent is ambiguous between model-checkpoint upgrade re-verification (ADR-006 CACHE_MIN_TOKENS), the contract hash pin (ADR-008), and the SDK+framework pin surface (ADR-015-3) — requires definition escalation before the checkpoint-compatibility wording can be authored.\\nGAP: manifest.yaml pins only docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md as references, but the request’s \\\"implemented pipeline status\\\" and current provider default live in code the manifest did not capture (config/settings.py, run.py, harness/claude_account_cli.py); the authoritative source for \\\"implemented\\\" reality is therefore only partially pinned.\\nGAP: host returned no file body for run.py, README.md, RUNBOOK.md, demo.py, releases/*, or tests/unit/test_run_cli.py despite read requests — the current wording those files must be reconciled from is unverified against the authority, so exact edit points are inferred, not confirmed.\\n\\n## Size estimate\\nA bounded documentation-and-help reconciliation touching ~5 surface files plus 1–2 enforcing tests and one release note; no runtime behaviour change. It fits the objective and does not need a split. The single genuine blocker is the undefined \\\"checkpoint compatibility rules\\\" term, which should be resolved by definition escalation rather than by inventing a rule.\\n\\n```yaml\\nsize_estimate:\\n  files: 6\\n  scale: medium          # small | medium | large\\n  subsystems: [docs, cli, releases, tests]\\n```\"}"},"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b2b2b893-f96b-442d-b34e-c844abfec356"}
